.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1206 AM PDT Sun Aug 9 2026
(Monday through Saturday)

Cooling trend kicks off Monday as upper-level shortwave troughing
develops off the West Coast. This will moderate temperatures to near
normal, deepen the marine layer bringing a chance for drizzle, and
increase onshore flow. A reinforcing trough Wednesday will bring
more prominent troughing off the West Coast Thursday and into the
weekend. This along with a resurgence in monsoonal moisture may be
enough to bring elevated rain showers/thunderstorms to the forecast.
While there`s no mention in the official forecast now, it may be
warranted as we get closer.

