.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 523 AM PDT Sun Aug 9 2026

A narrow channel of coastal stratus, fog and mist /MVFR-IFR-LIFR/
have held together and remains trapped beneath a strong lower level
temperature inversion associated with a strong 500 mb high pressure
system. Part of this stratus, fog and mist has reached into the Bay
Area and the north Central Coast. The marine layer depth is approx
1000 feet.

Satellite shows an area of clear sky out over the outer waters and
offshore waters which corresponds to an area of warmer air, primarily
drifting southward. Satellite also shows stratus and fog redeveloping
to our north. The leading edge of this stratus may join the nearly
stationary stratus south of Point Arena during and just after daybreak.
This pattern is characterized by large temperature differences over
short distances, mainly in the vertical and also from the coastline
to inland valleys (sharply warmer aloft, at the August maximum
otherwise not atypical of either July or August). It`s noteworthy
that air temperatures in the lower level temperature inversion are
in the 80s and lower 90s. With the wind flow weighted to onshore,
we`re essentially in a persistence forecast. Diurnal surface
warming will tap the lower level temperature inversion warmth,
vertical mixing and warming will mix out the stratus, fog and mist
to VFR back to the coastline today. The gradient of surface
pressure remains weighted to some northerly (ACV-SFO) otherwise
onshore per NAM output showing 4 mb to almost 5 mb SFO-SAC during
the afternoon and evening.

Depending how well (or not) the coastal stratus to our north holds
together during mixing today will determine if coastal stratus,
fog and mist return tonight and Monday morning. The NAM has been
verifying a little better than the HRRR model on this forecast.
The NAM leans toward stratus, fog and mist returning tonight and
Monday morning.

Recent GFS/NAM/HRRR output has also showed mid level instability
arriving from southern California approx Monday timeframe, but it
appears to dissipate while running northward into the strong ridge
and mid level dry air just to our north.

Vicinity of SFO...Stratus /IFR/ forecast mix out time is 17z
today. VFR for the remainder of the day then stratus is forecast
to return 10z Monday. West to northwest wind 5 to 15 knots except
15 to 25 knots this afternoon and evening.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Stratus, fog and mist /IFR-LIFR/ mixing
out to MVFR-VFR by late morning. Stratus, fog and mist /IFR-LIFR/
returns tonight and Monday morning. Mainly west to northwest winds
5 to 15 knots.

